+  o Minor features (onion service directory, DoS):
+    - HSDirs can now refuse onion service descriptor fetches and uploads whose
+      previous hop is not a known relay (in the consensus or with a
+      descriptor), and count the rest. Anyone can authenticate with a
+      self-generated relay key, so such requests could be single hop, which
+      HSDirs have refused from clients since 0.4.2.1-alpha. This rejects
+      arbitrary unknown prev-hop identities; it does not rate limit, since an
+      attacker can add one hop through any consensus relay. Refusing is off by
+      default (counting only): it is the new HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop torrc
+      option and "hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop" consensus parameter, both
+      independent of RefuseUnknownExits. The only false positives are in the
+      roughly 1e-6 per-request window when a relay has not yet seen the
+      previous hop in a fresh consensus. Part of ticket 41339.
diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index 0c029d1..2051750 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -3177,6 +3177,20 @@ The following options are useful only for an onion service directory (HSDir).
     operator or authority can measure the effect before enabling enforcement.
     (Default: auto)
 
+[[HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop]] **HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Since 0.4.2.1-alpha an HSDir refuses onion service descriptor fetches and
+    uploads from client channels, so they can't be made over one-hop circuits.
+    But a peer can authenticate with any self-generated relay identity, which
+    is not a client channel. If set to 1, an HSDir refuses (with a 503) such a
+    request whose previous hop is not a relay in its consensus or for which it
+    has a descriptor; if 0, it only counts them. "auto" means use the
+    hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop consensus parameter, and only count if the
+    consensus is silent. This option, and that parameter, are independent of
+    RefuseUnknownExits, so turning this off does not weaken exit protection.
+    The count appears in the heartbeat and as
+    tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}. (Default: auto)
+
 
 For onion services, mitigations are a work in progress and multiple options
 are currently available.
